Subject: [PATCH] hls: time renditions against one MPEG time reference

hlsdemux times a fragment that starts a stream, or follows a discontinuity
or a variant switch, by its position in the playlist. The positions sum up
the rounded EXTINF durations of each playlist on its own. A rendition with
its own playlist drifts against the variant: ZDF lists its packed audio
segments as 2.005 s, 2.000 s on average, and the audio came up to 200 ms
early, depending on where playback started.

Keep one reference of a stream time and an MPEG time, the first PCR of an
MPEG-TS fragment or the ID3 PTS of packed audio, and time such fragments of
all streams by their MPEG time against it. The first stream sets it; a
rendition adds a second so the variant does not start before the segment.
A seek, a reset and a discontinuity of the variant playlist clear it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
